STOP — there is no `scratchpad/` directory, by design.

This is a FILE, not a directory, on purpose: it holds the name `scratchpad`
so `mkdir scratchpad` fails (File exists) and `scratchpad/foo.wat` fails
(Not a directory). The dead scratch dir cannot be recreated — a structural
block, not a convention.

Scratch goes here instead:
  • throwaway / reconnaissance .wat  → wat-scripts/scratch-pad/**.wat
      Loader-gated: every .wat under wat-scripts/ is parsed + type-checked by
      the `every_wat_scripts_file_loads` test, so a scratch .wat that rots goes
      RED — it can never become a graveyard that reads like live code. All wat
      stays correct, always. (Per-file check: `target/release/wat --check f.wat`
      — the same load verdict in ~0.2s.)
  • non-.wat temp files (logs, patches, data) → the session scratchpad
      (/tmp/claude-.../scratchpad), never the repo.

